#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:2
msgid "set_color - set the terminal color"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:5
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:12
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:14
msgid ""
"``set_color`` is used to control the color and styling of text in the "
"terminal. *VALUE* describes that styling. *VALUE* can be a reserved color"
" name like **red** or an RGB color value given as 3 or 6 hexadecimal "
"digits (\"F27\" or \"FF2277\"). A special keyword **normal** resets text "
"formatting to terminal defaults, however it is not recommended and the "
"**--reset** option is preferred as it is less confusing and more future-"
"proof."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:19
msgid "Valid colors include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:21
msgid ""
"**black**, **red**, **green**, **yellow**, **blue**, **magenta**, "
"**cyan**, **white**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:22
msgid ""
"**brblack**, **brred**, **brgreen**, **bryellow**, **brblue**, "
"**brmagenta**, **brcyan**, **brwhite**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:24
msgid ""
"The *br*- (as in 'bright') forms are full-brightness variants of the 8 "
"standard-brightness colors on many terminals. **brblack** has higher "
"brightness than **black** - towards gray."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:26
msgid ""
"An RGB value with three or six hex digits, such as A0FF33 or f2f can be "
"used. A three digit value is equivalent to specifying each digit twice; "
"e.g., ``set_color 2BC`` is the same as ``set_color 22BBCC``. Hexadecimal "
"RGB values can be in lower or uppercase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:30
msgid ""
"If :envvar:`fish_term24bit` is set to 0, fish will translate RGB values "
"to the nearest color on the 256-color palette. If :envvar:`fish_term256` "
"is also set to 0, fish will translate them to the 16-color palette "
"instead. Fish launched as ``fish -d term_support`` will include "
"diagnostic messages that indicate the color support mode in use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:34
msgid ""
"If multiple colors are specified, fish prefers the first RGB one. However"
" if :envvar:`fish_term256` is set to 0, fish prefers the first named "
"color specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:37
msgid "The following options are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:39
msgid "**-f** or **--foreground** *COLOR*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:40
msgid ""
"Sets the foreground color. This is equivalent to calling ``set_color "
"COLOR`` with the exception that the keyword **normal** will only reset "
"the foreground color to its default, instead of all colors and modes. It "
"cannot be used with *VALUE* or **--print-colors**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:44
msgid "**-b** or **--background** *COLOR*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:45
msgid "Sets the background color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:47
msgid "**--underline-color** *COLOR*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:48
msgid "Set the underline color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:50
msgid "**-c** or **--print-colors**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:51
msgid ""
"Prints the given colors or a colored list of the 16 named colors. It "
"cannot be used with **--foreground**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:54
msgid "**-o** or **--bold**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:55
msgid "Sets bold mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:57
msgid "**-d** or **--dim**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:58
msgid "Sets dim mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:60
msgid "**-i** or **--italics**, or **-iSTATE** or **--italics=STATE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:61
msgid "Sets italics mode. The state can be **on** (default), or **off**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:63
msgid "**-r** or **--reverse**, or **-iSTATE** or **--reverse=STATE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:64
msgid "Sets reverse mode. The state can be **on** (default), or **off**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:66
msgid "**-s** or **--strikethrough**, or **-sSTATE** or **--strikethrough=STATE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:67
msgid "Sets strikethrough mode. The state can be **on** (default), or **off**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:69
msgid "**-u** or **--underline**, or **-uSTYLE** or **--underline=STYLE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:70
msgid ""
"Set the underline mode; supported styles are **single** (default), "
"**double**, **curly**, **dotted**, **dashed** and **off**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:72
msgid "**--reset**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:73
msgid ""
"Reset the text formatting to the terminal defaults before applying the "
"new colors and modes. This is equivalent to calling ``set_color normal`` "
"except that it is possible to set the foreground color in the same call "
"(e.g. ``set_color --reset green``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:76
msgid "**--theme=THEME**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:77
msgid ""
"Ignored. :ref:`Color variables <variables-color>` that contain only this "
"option are treated like missing / empty color variables, i.e. fish will "
"use the fallback color instead. :doc:`fish_config theme choose "
"<fish_config>` erases all :ref:`color variable <fish_config-color-"
"variables>` whose value includes this option, and adds this option to all"
" color variables it sets. This allows identifying variables set by a "
"theme, and it allows fish to update color variables whenever "
":envvar:`fish_terminal_color_theme` changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:85
msgid "**-h** or **--help**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:86
msgid "Displays help about using this command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:89
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:91
msgid ""
"Using ``set_color normal`` will reset all colors and modes to the "
"terminal's default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:92
msgid ""
"In contrast, ``set_color --foreground normal`` will only reset the "
"foreground color and leave all the other colors and modes unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:93
msgid ""
"Because of the risk of confusion, ``set_color --reset`` is recommended "
"over ``set_color normal``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:94
msgid ""
"Setting the background color only affects subsequently written "
"characters. Fish provides no way to set the background color for the "
"entire terminal window. Configuring the window background color (and "
"other attributes such as its opacity) has to be done using whatever "
"mechanisms the terminal provides. Look for a config option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:95
msgid ""
"Some terminals use the ``--bold`` escape sequence to switch to a brighter"
" color set rather than increasing the weight of text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/cmds/set_color.rst:96
msgid ""
"``set_color`` works by printing sequences of characters to standard "
"output. If used in command substitution or a pipe, these characters will "
"also be captured. This may or may not be desirable. Checking the exit "
"status of ``isatty stdout`` before using ``set_color`` can be useful to "
"decide not to colorize output in a script."
msgstr ""

